  "derivation": "Foundation 24 managed descriptors. Contract rows come from the pinned public metadata and from docs/generated/xna-il-inventory.json. Mapping rows encode what the pinned IL establishes: AudioListener and AudioEmitter pass every Vector3 through UnsafeNativeStructures::FlipHandedness, which is (X, Y, -Z), on both the getter and the setter, and their constructors store Position and Velocity unflipped but Forward and Up flipped, so the default Position and Velocity read back with a negative-zero Z while Forward and Up read back exactly; AudioEmitter.DopplerScale rejects only an ordered negative value because the guard is bge.un, so NaN is accepted; PresentationParameters' constructor performs exactly one store, set_IsFullScreen(true), leaving every other field at the CLR default, validates nothing, derives Bounds from the back buffer and clones by copying the whole settings struct. None is snapshotted from the cna-ruby implementation.",
